1 Introduction

The latest generation of video games has demonstrated a trend for producing realistic experiences through “natural” interaction techniques. Nintendo's Wii gaming console started this trend by providing the Wii Remote to mimic actions like swinging a tennis racket. Continuing the trend, Microsoft introduced Project Natal and the concept of controller-free gaming at E3 2009. With Project Natal, players can use their entire bodies to interact, such as making throwing motions to splash paint onto a canvas.
